--!strict
--[[
	Content/ContentQuery — pure queries over the AI Kingdoms content library
	(ReplicatedStorage.Game.Content, CONTRACTS G1). HAND-WRITTEN. Its siblings Dialogue, Decisions,
	Consequences, Traits, Occupations and Reputation are GENERATED by tools/content/content.py from
	games/game-001/content (schema: content/SPEC.md §7; effect model: SPEC §6). It implements FORGE-00
	model decisions 2–5 and the runtime half of the condition language (SPEC §4). No services, no
	yields, no randomness, no clock: every function returns the same answer for the same arguments.
	Callers pass `now` themselves (server time, CONTRACTS G13.4); a nil, NaN or infinite `now` is an
	error, because it would silently switch anti-farming off.

	Content is read-only. The generated modules are deeply frozen, and ContentQuery.new(data) deeply
	freezes the tables it is given (also inside tables that were frozen only at the top, and once each, so
	a cycle is safe), so every shared record ContentQuery returns (scenarios, action rows) errors when
	written to. Everything else it returns is a fresh table the caller owns.

	API (module functions use the generated content; ContentQuery.new(data) binds the same API to
	other tables of the generated shape, e.g. spec fixtures)

	Conditions and scenarios
		ContentQuery.evaluate(clauses: { Clause }?, ctx: Ctx?) -> boolean
			AND of every clause; nil/empty = true. Clause = { var, op, value } as generated.
			ctx is flat and keyed by variable name, e.g. ctx["kingdom.fed_ratio"]. Never errors.
			  - value is a boolean (bare `x` = { op "=", value true }, `!x` = { op "=", value false }):
			    the variable is a flag and an absent (nil) flag is false, so the runtime only needs to
			    set the flags that are true (memories, decisions, events, traits, has_*).
			  - an absent `kingdom.count.<type>` counts as 0 (no building of that type yet).
			  - any other clause on an absent (nil) variable is false, including "!=" and "in".
			  - "<" "<=" ">" ">=" need two numbers (no string-to-number coercion; NaN is false).
			  - "=" / "!=" compare type and value ("5" ~= 5). "in" = equal to one list item.
			  - an unknown op is false.
		ContentQuery.eligibleScenarios(ctx, citizen: CitizenState, now: number, history: ShownHistory?)
			-> { Scenario }
			Scenarios this citizen may be offered now: occupation is "any" or the citizen's occupation
			(citizen.occupation, else ctx.occupation); not `locked`, or unlocked for this citizen
			(citizen.unlocked[scenarioId] == true, set when an unlock_scenario consequence reaches
			them); trigger holds; not shown before when once_per_citizen; at least cooldown_s seconds
			since last shown (now - last >= cooldown_s). Sorted by priority (high first), then file
			order. The records are the shared, frozen content tables.
			The citizen is keyed in `history` by citizenKey(citizen): `id`, else `entityId` (G13.2
			CitizenView), else `key` (FORGE-01 Population.Citizen). Passing a history for a citizen
			with none of the three is an error (cooldowns would be ignored). A nil citizen or a bad
			`now` is an error.
			ShownHistory = { [citizenKey]: { [scenarioId]: lastShownTime } }, one per kingdom (SPEC §6.8).
		ContentQuery.citizenKey(citizen) -> any?        citizen.id, else entityId, else key
		ContentQuery.markShown(history, citizenKey, scenarioId, now) -> history     records a showing
			(pass citizenKey(citizen), so eligibleScenarios finds it). A nil history, citizenKey or bad
			`now` is an error.
		ContentQuery.choicePreview(scenarioId, responseId) -> ChoicePreview?
			{ decision, cost, risks } of one answer, for the conversation panel: the cost and the
			chance < 1 consequences the player must see before choosing (model decision 7).

	Decisions (dialogue)
		ContentQuery.decisionEffects(decisionId, multiplier: number?, kingdomMultiplier: number?) -> Effects?
			A fresh copy of the decision's effect bundle (nil for an unknown id), for previews.
			`multiplier` is the ruler's anti-farming multiplier (default 1): it scales reputation GAINS
			in `rep`. `kingdomMultiplier` (default = multiplier) scales every other gain: kingdom
			happiness/stability/morale, speaker chemistry, the explicit loyalty columns, and gain
			consequences (loyalty, morale, happiness, stability > 0; unrest_pressure < 0, i.e. relief).
			Losses are never reduced. `speaker.loyalty`, `family_loyalty`, `friends_loyalty`,
			`rivals_loyalty` and `audience_loyalty` are the change of a listener with no personality
			reaction (no traits, chemistry 0): the column, gains × kingdomMultiplier, clamped by
			LOYALTY_CLAMP. The raw columns are in `loyalty_raw` and the raw reputation vector (the one
			personalities react to) in `rep_raw`. `risks` are the consequences with chance < 1.
		ContentQuery.fireDecision(decisionId, rulerHistory: FarmHistory, kingdomHistory: FarmHistory, now,
			listeners: { DecisionListener }?) -> Effects?
			The single anti-farming point of a dialogue choice (CONTRACTS G13.1). Call it once per choice,
			AFTER the cost was paid (TreasuryService): a refused payment must not record a firing. It
			takes both multipliers from the decision's farm_key/repeat_decay/repeat_window_s (ruler
			history for reputation, kingdom history for everything else), records the firing in both
			histories and returns decisionEffects(id, rulerMultiplier, kingdomMultiplier) plus
			`listeners`: one { citizen, relation, loyalty } per given listener
			(DecisionListener = { citizen, relation, traits, chemistry? }), loyalty =
			decisionLoyalty(id, traits, relation, chemistry, kingdomMultiplier). Everything in the
			result is APPLIED AS GIVEN: no second decay, no second clamp (ReputationService included).
			`cost` is informational (already paid). Each listener once, under its closest relation
			(speaker > family > friends > rivals > kingdom); a listener's change is its `loyalty`, never
			loyalty plus the explicit column. Every listener is checked first (a traits list of known
			trait ids, a known relation): an error names the listener (`listener #i has an unknown
			trait ...`) and records nothing. Unknown decision: nil and nothing recorded.
		ContentQuery.loyaltyDelta(rep: RepVector, traits: { string }, relation: Relation,
			chemistry: number?, extra: number?) -> number
			Model decisions 3–4, a building block (no decay, no clamp): (Σ_category Σ_trait weight ×
			rep[c]) × REACH[relation] + extra, then gains × (1 + chemistry/40) and losses ×
			(1 − chemistry/40), chemistry clamped to ±20. `extra` is a flat delta added before the
			chemistry factor (explicit columns and trait overrides). Missing rep categories are 0.
			Unknown trait or relation: error. Trait weights are Traits[traitId].weights[category].
		ContentQuery.decisionLoyalty(decisionId, traits, relation, chemistry?, multiplier?) -> number
			One listener's applied loyalty change for a dialogue decision: loyaltyDelta(rep_raw, ...)
			with extra = the relation's column (speaker.loyalty, family_loyalty, friends_loyalty,
			rivals_loyalty, or audience_loyalty for "kingdom") + the listener's trait_overrides, then
			a gain × multiplier (losses unchanged, model decision 5; pass the kingdom multiplier), then
			clamped to ±LOYALTY_CLAMP[relation] (FORGE-00 decision M3). Relation "kingdom" means a
			member of the decision's audience with no closer tie (the runtime filters the audience:
			the speaker's occupation for "occupation", everyone for "kingdom"); it is 0 when the
			audience is "none".

	Actions (non-dialogue ruler acts, SPEC §6.9)
		ContentQuery.fireAction(event, ctx: Ctx?, rulerHistory, kingdomHistory, now,
			listeners: { ActionListener }?) -> { ActionEffects }
			The single anti-farming point of actions.csv (mirrors fireDecision). One entry per firing
			of actionFirings(event, ctx), in file order. Each firing takes its multipliers from its
			farm_key (ruler history: reputation; kingdom history: loyalty and kingdom conditions) and
			records itself in both histories before the next firing is computed. `rep` = the sum over
			its rows of each row's rep with gains × ruler multiplier, `kingdom` = the same with the
			kingdom multiplier: each row is decayed on its own, then summed, so one row's loss is never
			decayed with another row's gain (model decision 5; the same rule as the listeners). Raw sums
			in `rep_raw`, `kingdom_raw`. `listeners`: every given listener who hears at least one row
			(ActionListener = { citizen, occupation?, speaker?, traits, chemistry?, ctx? }) as
			{ citizen, relation, loyalty }: the sum over the rows it hears of actionLoyalty before the
			clamp (gains × kingdom multiplier), clamped once to LOYALTY_CLAMP of its relation ("speaker"
			when it hears a speaker row, else "kingdom"). Apply as given.
		ContentQuery.actionFirings(event: string, ctx: Ctx?) -> { ActionFiring }
			The rows that apply when `event` fires ("Name:arg" also matches rows of the bare "Name"),
			filtered by their kingdom `condition`, grouped per action id in file order. Each firing
			is one anti-farming firing of its farm_key. `rep` and `kingdom` are the raw sums of its
			rows (fireAction decays them).
		ContentQuery.inActionAudience(row: ActionRow, listener: Listener, listenerCtx: Ctx?) -> boolean
			Whether a citizen hears this row: audience "kingdom" = everyone; "soldiers" = occupation
			whose job is soldier (captain included); "civilians" = everyone else; "occupation:<id>";
			"speaker" = listener.speaker; then the row's audience_condition on listenerCtx.
		ContentQuery.actionLoyalty(row: ActionRow, traits, chemistry?, multiplier?) -> number
			One listener's loyalty change from one row: loyaltyDelta(row.rep, traits, reach "speaker"
			for audience speaker, else "kingdom", chemistry, row.audience_loyalty), gain × multiplier,
			clamped like fireAction. 0 without an audience. A listener who hears several rows of one
			firing: use fireAction (it sums the rows first, then clamps once).

	Anti-farming and helpers
		ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(history: FarmHistory?, farmKey, now, decay?, window?) -> number
			Model decision 5: decay ^ (earlier firings of farmKey with now − t < window), i.e. the
			n-th firing inside the window gets decay^(n−1). decay is clamped to [0, 1]; window <= 0
			or decay 1 gives 1. FarmHistory = { [farmKey]: { fireTime } }: one per ruler (reputation)
			and one per kingdom (loyalty and kingdom conditions), SPEC §6.8. A building block: its
			history is optional, and nil means no earlier firings (1). fireDecision, fireAction,
			recordFire and markShown require theirs.
		ContentQuery.recordFire(history, farmKey, now) -> history
			Appends a firing; keeps the newest MAX_FARM_HISTORY per key. A nil history is an error.
		ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta, multiplier) -> number     delta > 0 → delta × multiplier
		ContentQuery.scaleGains(vector, multiplier) -> vector   scaleGain on every entry (a copy)
		ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(delta, relation) -> number     ±LOYALTY_CLAMP[relation]; NaN → 0
		ContentQuery.applyChemistry(delta, chemistry?) -> number model decision 4 on one delta
		ContentQuery.startLoyalty(chemistry?) -> integer
			Model decision 2: math.floor(50 + chemistry/4 + 0.5), chemistry clamped to ±20 (45..55).
			CitizenService uses this for every generated citizen (FORGE-00 decision L12).
		ContentQuery.driftChemistry(base, current, delta) -> number
			current + delta, kept within base ± CHEMISTRY_DRIFT_MAX and −20..+20: decisions may move
			the chemistry rolled at generation by at most 5 over a match (SPEC §6.4).
		ContentQuery.noticeValues(consequence) -> { [string]: string }
			The mechanics placeholders of a consequence notice: chance "50%", magnitude "+5" / "-4",
			magnitude_pct "15%" (absolute), duration "45 s" / "2 minutes".
		ContentQuery.fill(text, values) -> string  replaces {key} for every key in values; leaves others
		ContentQuery.consequenceNotice(consequence, names?) -> string?
			fill(notice, names + noticeValues), names = { name =, ruler =, kingdom =, occupation = }.
			The mechanics values are applied last, so a name can never override the real odds.
		ContentQuery.durationText(seconds) -> string
		ContentQuery.REACH          { speaker 1, family 0.6, friends 0.4, rivals −0.3, kingdom 0.2 } (frozen)
		ContentQuery.LOYALTY_CLAMP  { speaker 25, family 10, friends 10, rivals 10, kingdom 5 } (frozen):
		                            the most a decision's own loyalty term (personality, explicit column,
		                            trait overrides) or one action firing may move one listener's loyalty,
		                            after chemistry and decay ("kingdom" = audience). Loyalty CONSEQUENCES
		                            (kind loyalty) are separate effects outside the clamp (SPEC §6.3)
		ContentQuery.CATEGORIES     the six reputation categories in canonical order (frozen)
		ContentQuery.OPS            the clause operators the generator emits (frozen set)
		ContentQuery.GAIN_SIGN      consequence kinds whose magnitude decays when it is a gain (frozen)
		ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MIN / CHEMISTRY_MAX (−20 / 20), CHEMISTRY_DRIFT_MAX (5), MAX_FARM_HISTORY (32)
		ContentQuery.new(data: DataInput) -> Query
			{ dialogue?, decisions?, consequences?, traits?, occupations?, reputation? } in the
			generated shapes (missing = empty), deeply frozen in place. Query has data and every
			function above.
]]

local Consequences = require("./Consequences")
local Decisions = require("./Decisions")
local Dialogue = require("./Dialogue")
local Occupations = require("./Occupations")
local Reputation = require("./Reputation")
local Traits = require("./Traits")

export type Clause = { var: string, op: string, value: any }
export type Ctx = { [string]: any }
export type RepVector = { [string]: number }
export type Relation = "speaker" | "family" | "friends" | "rivals" | "kingdom"
export type KingdomDelta = { happiness: number, stability: number, morale: number }

export type Response = {
	id: string,
	order: number,
	text: string,
	reaction: string,
	tone: string?,
	decision: string,
}
export type Scenario = {
	id: string,
	occupation: string,
	trigger: { Clause },
	priority: number,
	cooldown_s: number,
	once_per_citizen: boolean,
	locked: boolean?,
	icon: string?,
	thought: string,
	question: string,
	responses: { Response },
}
export type DialogueData = { scenarios: { [string]: Scenario }, order: { string } }

export type Decision = {
	id: string,
	farm_key: string,
	repeat_decay: number,
	repeat_window_s: number,
	cost: { [string]: number },
	resources: { [string]: number },
	rep: RepVector,
	speaker: { loyalty: number, chemistry: number },
	family_loyalty: number,
	friends_loyalty: number,
	rivals_loyalty: number,
	audience: string,
	audience_loyalty: number,
	kingdom: KingdomDelta,
	trait_overrides: { [string]: number },
	consequences: { string },
	memory_tag: string?,
}

export type Consequence = {
	id: string,
	kind: string,
	target: string,
	magnitude: number,
	duration_s: number,
	delay_s: number,
	chance: number,
	param: string?,
	cue_id: string?,
	notice: string?,
}

export type Trait = {
	id: string,
	name: string,
	description: string,
	opposite: string?,
	weights: RepVector,
	obedience_bias: number,
	productivity: number,
	hunger_sensitivity: number,
	gossip: number,
	volatility: number,
}

export type Occupation = {
	id: string,
	name: string,
	job: string,
	key_role: string?,
	needs: { string },
	trait_affinity: { [string]: number },
}

export type ActionRow = {
	id: string,
	event: string,
	condition: { Clause },
	farm_key: string,
	repeat_decay: number,
	repeat_window_s: number,
	rep: RepVector,
	audience: string?,
	audience_condition: { Clause },
	audience_loyalty: number,
	kingdom: KingdomDelta,
	notice: string?,
}
export type ReputationData = {
	categories: { [string]: any },
	order: { string },
	actions: { ActionRow },
	byEvent: { [string]: { number } },
}
export type ActionFiring = {
	id: string,
	farm_key: string,
	repeat_decay: number,
	repeat_window_s: number,
	rows: { ActionRow },
	rep: RepVector,
	kingdom: KingdomDelta,
}

export type Data = {
	dialogue: DialogueData,
	decisions: { [string]: Decision },
	consequences: { [string]: Consequence },
	traits: { [string]: Trait },
	occupations: { [string]: Occupation },
	reputation: ReputationData,
}
export type DataInput = {
	dialogue: DialogueData?,
	decisions: { [string]: Decision }?,
	consequences: { [string]: Consequence }?,
	traits: { [string]: Trait }?,
	occupations: { [string]: Occupation }?,
	reputation: ReputationData?,
}

-- The citizen's key for ShownHistory is `id`, else `entityId` (G13.2 CitizenView), else `key` (FORGE-01).
export type CitizenState = {
	id: any?,
	entityId: any?,
	key: any?,
	occupation: string?,
	unlocked: { [string]: boolean }?,
}
export type Listener = { occupation: string?, speaker: boolean? }
export type ShownHistory = { [any]: { [string]: number } }
export type FarmHistory = { [string]: { number } }

-- A citizen who hears a decision: `citizen` is the caller's key, echoed in the result.
export type DecisionListener = { citizen: any, relation: Relation, traits: { string }, chemistry: number? }
-- A citizen who may hear an action: occupation/speaker pick the audience, ctx is its audience_condition ctx.
export type ActionListener = {
	citizen: any,
	occupation: string?,
	speaker: boolean?,
	traits: { string },
	chemistry: number?,
	ctx: Ctx?,
}
-- One listener's loyalty change, final: decayed and clamped. Apply as given.
export type ListenerLoyalty = { citizen: any, relation: Relation, loyalty: number }
export type LoyaltyColumns = { speaker: number, family: number, friends: number, rivals: number, audience: number }

export type Effects = {
	id: string,
	farm_key: string,
	repeat_decay: number,
	repeat_window_s: number,
	multiplier: number,
	kingdom_multiplier: number,
	cost: { [string]: number },
	resources: { [string]: number },
	rep: RepVector,
	rep_raw: RepVector,
	speaker: { loyalty: number, chemistry: number },
	family_loyalty: number,
	friends_loyalty: number,
	rivals_loyalty: number,
	audience: string,
	audience_loyalty: number,
	kingdom: KingdomDelta,
	trait_overrides: { [string]: number },
	loyalty_raw: LoyaltyColumns,
	consequences: { Consequence },
	risks: { Consequence },
	memory_tag: string?,
	listeners: { ListenerLoyalty },
}
export type ActionEffects = {
	id: string,
	event: string,
	farm_key: string,
	repeat_decay: number,
	repeat_window_s: number,
	multiplier: number,
	kingdom_multiplier: number,
	rows: { ActionRow },
	rep: RepVector,
	rep_raw: RepVector,
	kingdom: KingdomDelta,
	kingdom_raw: KingdomDelta,
	listeners: { ListenerLoyalty },
}
export type ChoicePreview = { decision: string, cost: { [string]: number }, risks: { Consequence } }

export type Query = {
	data: Data,
	eligibleScenarios: (ctx: Ctx?, citizen: CitizenState, now: number, history: ShownHistory?) -> { Scenario },
	choicePreview: (scenarioId: string, responseId: string) -> ChoicePreview?,
	decisionEffects: (decisionId: string, multiplier: number?, kingdomMultiplier: number?) -> Effects?,
	fireDecision: (
		decisionId: string,
		rulerHistory: FarmHistory,
		kingdomHistory: FarmHistory,
		now: number,
		listeners: { DecisionListener }?
	) -> Effects?,
	fireAction: (
		event: string,
		ctx: Ctx?,
		rulerHistory: FarmHistory,
		kingdomHistory: FarmHistory,
		now: number,
		listeners: { ActionListener }?
	) -> { ActionEffects },
	loyaltyDelta: (
		rep: RepVector,
		traits: { string },
		relation: Relation,
		chemistry: number?,
		extra: number?
	) -> number,
	decisionLoyalty: (
		decisionId: string,
		traits: { string },
		relation: Relation,
		chemistry: number?,
		multiplier: number?
	) -> number,
	actionFirings: (event: string, ctx: Ctx?) -> { ActionFiring },
	inActionAudience: (row: ActionRow, listener: Listener, listenerCtx: Ctx?) -> boolean,
	actionLoyalty: (row: ActionRow, traits: { string }, chemistry: number?, multiplier: number?) -> number,
	evaluate: (clauses: { Clause }?, ctx: Ctx?) -> boolean,
	repeatMultiplier: (
		history: FarmHistory?,
		farmKey: string,
		now: number,
		decay: number?,
		window: number?
	) -> number,
	recordFire: (history: FarmHistory, farmKey: string, now: number) -> FarmHistory,
	markShown: (history: ShownHistory, citizenId: any, scenarioId: string, now: number) -> ShownHistory,
	citizenKey: (citizen: CitizenState) -> any,
	clampLoyalty: (delta: number, relation: Relation) -> number,
	scaleGain: (delta: number, multiplier: number) -> number,
	scaleGains: (vector: { [string]: number }, multiplier: number) -> { [string]: number },
	applyChemistry: (delta: number, chemistry: number?) -> number,
	startLoyalty: (chemistry: number?) -> number,
	driftChemistry: (base: number, current: number, delta: number) -> number,
	noticeValues: (consequence: Consequence) -> { [string]: string },
	fill: (text: string, values: { [string]: string }) -> string,
	consequenceNotice: (consequence: Consequence, names: { [string]: string }?) -> string?,
	durationText: (seconds: number) -> string,
}

local ContentQuery = {}

ContentQuery.CATEGORIES = table.freeze({ "compassion", "honor", "competence", "courage", "authority", "fear" })
ContentQuery.REACH = table.freeze({ speaker = 1, family = 0.6, friends = 0.4, rivals = -0.3, kingdom = 0.2 })
ContentQuery.OPS = table.freeze({
	["="] = true,
	["!="] = true,
	["<"] = true,
	["<="] = true,
	[">"] = true,
	[">="] = true,
	["in"] = true,
})
-- Consequence kinds whose magnitude is a gain for the ruler when magnitude × sign > 0 (decayed by the
-- kingdom multiplier, model decision 5 as extended in SPEC §6.5). unrest_pressure relief is negative.
ContentQuery.GAIN_SIGN = table.freeze({ loyalty = 1, morale = 1, happiness = 1, stability = 1, unrest_pressure = -1 })
-- FORGE-00 decision M3: the most one decision's own loyalty term (or one action firing) may move one listener's
-- loyalty, applied after the personality term, chemistry and decay. "kingdom" is any audience listener without a
-- closer tie. Loyalty consequences are separate effects with their own validated magnitude (SPEC §6.3).
ContentQuery.LOYALTY_CLAMP = table.freeze({ speaker = 25, family = 10, friends = 10, rivals = 10, kingdom = 5 })
ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MIN = -20
ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MAX = 20
ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_DRIFT_MAX = 5
ContentQuery.MAX_FARM_HISTORY = 32

local CATEGORIES = ContentQuery.CATEGORIES
local REACH: { [string]: number } = ContentQuery.REACH
local LOYALTY_CLAMP: { [string]: number } = ContentQuery.LOYALTY_CLAMP
local GAIN_SIGN: { [string]: number } = ContentQuery.GAIN_SIGN
local COUNT_PREFIX = "kingdom.count."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- argument checks

-- A nil, NaN or infinite `now` would silently disable cooldowns and anti-farming (review finding L9).
local function checkNow(fn: string, now: any)
	if type(now) ~= "number" or now ~= now or now == math.huge or now == -math.huge then
		error(`ContentQuery.{fn}: now must be a finite number (server time), got {tostring(now)}`, 3)
	end
end

local function checkHistory(fn: string, name: string, history: any, kind: string?)
	if type(history) ~= "table" then
		error(`ContentQuery.{fn}: {name} must be a {kind or "FarmHistory"} table, got {typeof(history)}`, 3)
	end
end

-- Content is shared and read-only: freeze every table reachable from `value`, children first (review finding L6).
-- A frozen table is still walked, because `table.freeze({ ... })` freezes only the top; `seen` visits each table
-- once, so a cycle cannot overflow the stack.
local function deepFreeze<T>(value: T, seen: { [any]: boolean }?): T
	local visited: { [any]: boolean } = seen or {}
	local t = value :: any
	if visited[t] then
		return value
	end
	visited[t] = true
	for _, child in t do
		if type(child) == "table" then
			deepFreeze(child, visited)
		end
	end
	if not table.isfrozen(t) then
		table.freeze(t)
	end
	return value
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- data-free functions

local function clauseHolds(clause: Clause, ctx: Ctx): boolean
	local actual = ctx[clause.var]
	local op, value = clause.op, clause.value
	if type(value) == "boolean" then
		-- A flag: absent means false (SPEC §4 normalises `x` / `!x` to "=" true / false).
		if actual == nil then
			actual = false
		end
		if op == "=" then
			return actual == value
		elseif op == "!=" then
			return actual ~= value
		end
		return false
	end
	if actual == nil then
		-- A building count the runtime did not set is 0 (SPEC §4), so "no smithy yet" works.
		if string.sub(clause.var, 1, #COUNT_PREFIX) ~= COUNT_PREFIX then
			return false
		end
		actual = 0
	end
	if op == "=" then
		return actual == value
	elseif op == "!=" then
		return actual ~= value
	elseif op == "in" then
		if type(value) ~= "table" then
			return false
		end
		for _, item in value do
			if item == actual then
				return true
			end
		end
		return false
	end
	if type(actual) ~= "number" or type(value) ~= "number" then
		return false
	end
	if op == "<" then
		return actual < value
	elseif op == "<=" then
		return actual <= value
	elseif op == ">" then
		return actual > value
	elseif op == ">=" then
		return actual >= value
	end
	return false
end

function ContentQuery.evaluate(clauses: { Clause }?, ctx: Ctx?): boolean
	if clauses == nil then
		return true
	end
	local c: Ctx = ctx or {}
	for _, clause in clauses do
		if not clauseHolds(clause, c) then
			return false
		end
	end
	return true
end

local function clampChemistry(chemistry: number?): number
	local c = chemistry or 0
	if c ~= c then
		return 0
	end
	return math.clamp(c, ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MIN, ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MAX)
end

function ContentQuery.applyChemistry(delta: number, chemistry: number?): number
	local c = clampChemistry(chemistry)
	if delta > 0 then
		return delta * (1 + c / 40)
	elseif delta < 0 then
		return delta * (1 - c / 40)
	end
	return 0
end

function ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta: number, multiplier: number): number
	if delta > 0 then
		return delta * multiplier
	end
	return delta
end

function ContentQuery.scaleGains(vector: { [string]: number }, multiplier: number): { [string]: number }
	local out = {}
	for key, delta in vector do
		out[key] = ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta, multiplier)
	end
	return out
end

function ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(delta: number, relation: Relation): number
	local limit = LOYALTY_CLAMP[relation]
	if limit == nil then
		error(`ContentQuery.clampLoyalty: unknown relation '{tostring(relation)}'`, 2)
	end
	if delta ~= delta then
		return 0
	end
	return math.clamp(delta, -limit, limit)
end

-- FORGE-00 decision L12: an integer start, rounded half up (the same formula as FORGE-01's generator).
function ContentQuery.startLoyalty(chemistry: number?): number
	return math.floor(50 + clampChemistry(chemistry) / 4 + 0.5)
end

function ContentQuery.driftChemistry(base: number, current: number, delta: number): number
	local b = clampChemistry(base)
	local lo = math.max(ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MIN, b - ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_DRIFT_MAX)
	local hi = math.min(ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_MAX, b + ContentQuery.CHEMISTRY_DRIFT_MAX)
	local value = current + delta
	if value ~= value then
		return b
	end
	return math.clamp(value, lo, hi)
end

function ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(
	history: FarmHistory?,
	farmKey: string,
	now: number,
	decay: number?,
	window: number?
): number
	checkNow("repeatMultiplier", now)
	local d = decay or 1
	if d ~= d then
		d = 1
	end
	d = math.clamp(d, 0, 1)
	local w = window or 0
	if d >= 1 or not (w > 0) or history == nil then
		return 1
	end
	local times = history[farmKey]
	if times == nil then
		return 1
	end
	local earlier = 0
	for _, t in times do
		if now - t < w then
			earlier += 1
		end
	end
	return d ^ earlier
end

function ContentQuery.recordFire(history: FarmHistory, farmKey: string, now: number): FarmHistory
	checkNow("recordFire", now)
	checkHistory("recordFire", "history", history)
	local times = history[farmKey]
	if times == nil then
		times = {}
		history[farmKey] = times
	end
	table.insert(times, now)
	while #times > ContentQuery.MAX_FARM_HISTORY do
		table.remove(times, 1)
	end
	return history
end

function ContentQuery.markShown(history: ShownHistory, citizenId: any, scenarioId: string, now: number): ShownHistory
	checkNow("markShown", now)
	checkHistory("markShown", "history", history, "ShownHistory")
	if citizenId == nil then
		error("ContentQuery.markShown: citizenId is nil (pass ContentQuery.citizenKey(citizen))", 2)
	end
	local shown = history[citizenId]
	if shown == nil then
		shown = {}
		history[citizenId] = shown
	end
	shown[scenarioId] = now
	return history
end

function ContentQuery.citizenKey(citizen: CitizenState): any
	if citizen.id ~= nil then
		return citizen.id
	elseif citizen.entityId ~= nil then
		return citizen.entityId
	end
	return citizen.key
end

function ContentQuery.durationText(seconds: number): string
	if seconds >= 60 and seconds % 60 == 0 then
		local minutes = seconds // 60
		return if minutes == 1 then "1 minute" else `{minutes} minutes`
	end
	return `{seconds} s`
end

local function percent(x: number): string
	return `{math.round(x * 100)}%`
end

local function signed(x: number): string
	if x == math.floor(x) then
		return string.format("%+d", x)
	end
	return string.format("%+g", x)
end

function ContentQuery.noticeValues(consequence: Consequence): { [string]: string }
	return {
		chance = percent(consequence.chance),
		magnitude = signed(consequence.magnitude),
		magnitude_pct = percent(math.abs(consequence.magnitude)),
		duration = ContentQuery.durationText(consequence.duration_s),
	}
end

function ContentQuery.fill(text: string, values: { [string]: string }): string
	-- A table replacement keeps the original "{key}" when values has no entry for key.
	local out = string.gsub(text, "{([%w_]+)}", values)
	return out
end

function ContentQuery.consequenceNotice(consequence: Consequence, names: { [string]: string }?): string?
	local notice = consequence.notice
	if notice == nil then
		return nil
	end
	-- names first, mechanics last: a name entry can never replace the real odds (review finding L8)
	local values: { [string]: string } = table.clone(names or {})
	for key, value in ContentQuery.noticeValues(consequence) do
		values[key] = value
	end
	return ContentQuery.fill(notice, values)
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- data-bound functions

local function copyMap<V>(t: { [string]: V }): { [string]: V }
	return table.clone(t)
end

local EMPTY_REPUTATION: ReputationData = deepFreeze({ categories = {}, order = {}, actions = {}, byEvent = {} })

function ContentQuery.new(input: DataInput): Query
	local data: Data = deepFreeze({
		dialogue = input.dialogue or { scenarios = {}, order = {} },
		decisions = input.decisions or {},
		consequences = input.consequences or {},
		traits = input.traits or {},
		occupations = input.occupations or {},
		reputation = input.reputation or EMPTY_REPUTATION,
	})
	local scenarios = data.dialogue.scenarios
	local fileIndex: { [string]: number } = {}
	for i, id in data.dialogue.order do
		fileIndex[id] = i
	end

	local query = {}
	query.data = data
	query.evaluate = ContentQuery.evaluate
	query.repeatMultiplier = ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier
	query.recordFire = ContentQuery.recordFire
	query.markShown = ContentQuery.markShown
	query.citizenKey = ContentQuery.citizenKey
	query.clampLoyalty = ContentQuery.clampLoyalty
	query.scaleGain = ContentQuery.scaleGain
	query.scaleGains = ContentQuery.scaleGains
	query.applyChemistry = ContentQuery.applyChemistry
	query.startLoyalty = ContentQuery.startLoyalty
	query.driftChemistry = ContentQuery.driftChemistry
	query.noticeValues = ContentQuery.noticeValues
	query.fill = ContentQuery.fill
	query.consequenceNotice = ContentQuery.consequenceNotice
	query.durationText = ContentQuery.durationText

	function query.eligibleScenarios(
		ctx: Ctx?,
		citizen: CitizenState,
		now: number,
		history: ShownHistory?
	): { Scenario }
		if type(citizen) ~= "table" then
			error(`ContentQuery.eligibleScenarios: citizen must be a CitizenState table, got {typeof(citizen)}`, 2)
		end
		checkNow("eligibleScenarios", now)
		local c: Ctx = ctx or {}
		local occupation = citizen.occupation or c.occupation
		local key = ContentQuery.citizenKey(citizen)
		if history ~= nil and key == nil then
			error(
				"ContentQuery.eligibleScenarios: the citizen has no id, entityId or key, so its shown-history "
					.. "(cooldowns, once_per_citizen) cannot be found",
				2
			)
		end
		local shown = if history then history[key] else nil
		local unlocked = citizen.unlocked
		local out: { Scenario } = {}
		for _, id in data.dialogue.order do
			local s = scenarios[id]
			if s == nil or (s.occupation ~= "any" and s.occupation ~= occupation) then
				continue
			end
			if s.locked and not (unlocked and unlocked[id] == true) then
				continue
			end
			local last = if shown then shown[id] else nil
			if last ~= nil and (s.once_per_citizen or now - last < s.cooldown_s) then
				continue
			end
			if ContentQuery.evaluate(s.trigger, c) then
				table.insert(out, s)
			end
		end
		table.sort(out, function(a: Scenario, b: Scenario): boolean
			if a.priority ~= b.priority then
				return a.priority > b.priority
			end
			return fileIndex[a.id] < fileIndex[b.id]
		end)
		return out
	end

	-- Every listener is checked before the first firing is recorded, so a bad listener records nothing and the
	-- error names the function and the listener. `relations`: whether each listener names a known relation.
	local function checkListeners(fn: string, listeners: { any }?, relations: boolean)
		for i, listener in listeners or {} do
			if type(listener) ~= "table" or type(listener.traits) ~= "table" then
				error(`ContentQuery.{fn}: listener #{i} must be a table with a traits list`, 3)
			end
			if relations and REACH[listener.relation] == nil then
				error(
					`ContentQuery.{fn}: listener #{i} has an unknown relation '{tostring(listener.relation)}' `
						.. "(speaker, family, friends, rivals or kingdom)",
					3
				)
			end
			for _, traitId in listener.traits do
				if data.traits[traitId] == nil then
					error(`ContentQuery.{fn}: listener #{i} has an unknown trait '{tostring(traitId)}'`, 3)
				end
			end
		end
	end

	-- An explicit loyalty column as a listener without a personality reaction gets it: decayed, then clamped.
	local function neutralLoyalty(raw: number, relation: Relation, kingdomMultiplier: number): number
		return ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(ContentQuery.scaleGain(raw, kingdomMultiplier), relation)
	end

	function query.decisionEffects(decisionId: string, multiplier: number?, kingdomMultiplier: number?): Effects?
		local d = data.decisions[decisionId]
		if d == nil then
			return nil
		end
		local m = multiplier or 1
		local km = kingdomMultiplier or m
		local rep: RepVector, raw: RepVector = {}, {}
		for _, category in CATEGORIES do
			local delta = d.rep[category] or 0
			raw[category] = delta
			rep[category] = ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta, m)
		end
		local consequences: { Consequence }, risks: { Consequence } = {}, {}
		for _, id in d.consequences do
			local record = data.consequences[id]
			if record == nil then
				error(`ContentQuery: decision '{decisionId}' references unknown consequence '{id}'`, 2)
			end
			local copy = table.clone(record)
			local sign = GAIN_SIGN[copy.kind]
			if sign ~= nil and copy.magnitude * sign > 0 then
				copy.magnitude *= km
			end
			table.insert(consequences, copy)
			if copy.chance < 1 then
				table.insert(risks, copy)
			end
		end
		return {
			id = d.id,
			farm_key = d.farm_key,
			repeat_decay = d.repeat_decay,
			repeat_window_s = d.repeat_window_s,
			multiplier = m,
			kingdom_multiplier = km,
			cost = copyMap(d.cost),
			resources = copyMap(d.resources),
			rep = rep,
			rep_raw = raw,
			speaker = {
				loyalty = neutralLoyalty(d.speaker.loyalty, "speaker", km),
				chemistry = ContentQuery.scaleGain(d.speaker.chemistry, km),
			},
			family_loyalty = neutralLoyalty(d.family_loyalty, "family", km),
			friends_loyalty = neutralLoyalty(d.friends_loyalty, "friends", km),
			rivals_loyalty = neutralLoyalty(d.rivals_loyalty, "rivals", km),
			audience = d.audience,
			audience_loyalty = neutralLoyalty(d.audience_loyalty, "kingdom", km),
			kingdom = {
				happiness = ContentQuery.scaleGain(d.kingdom.happiness, km),
				stability = ContentQuery.scaleGain(d.kingdom.stability, km),
				morale = ContentQuery.scaleGain(d.kingdom.morale, km),
			},
			trait_overrides = copyMap(d.trait_overrides),
			loyalty_raw = {
				speaker = d.speaker.loyalty,
				family = d.family_loyalty,
				friends = d.friends_loyalty,
				rivals = d.rivals_loyalty,
				audience = d.audience_loyalty,
			},
			consequences = consequences,
			risks = risks,
			memory_tag = d.memory_tag,
			listeners = {},
		}
	end

	function query.fireDecision(
		decisionId: string,
		rulerHistory: FarmHistory,
		kingdomHistory: FarmHistory,
		now: number,
		listeners: { DecisionListener }?
	): Effects?
		checkHistory("fireDecision", "rulerHistory", rulerHistory)
		checkHistory("fireDecision", "kingdomHistory", kingdomHistory)
		checkNow("fireDecision", now)
		checkListeners("fireDecision", listeners, true)
		local d = data.decisions[decisionId]
		if d == nil then
			return nil
		end
		local key, decay, window = d.farm_key, d.repeat_decay, d.repeat_window_s
		local m = ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(rulerHistory, key, now, decay, window)
		local km = ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(kingdomHistory, key, now, decay, window)
		-- compute before recording, so an unexpected error records nothing
		local effects = query.decisionEffects(decisionId, m, km)
		assert(effects, "decision exists")
		for _, listener in listeners or {} do
			table.insert(effects.listeners, {
				citizen = listener.citizen,
				relation = listener.relation,
				loyalty = query.decisionLoyalty(decisionId, listener.traits, listener.relation, listener.chemistry, km),
			})
		end
		ContentQuery.recordFire(rulerHistory, key, now)
		if kingdomHistory ~= rulerHistory then
			ContentQuery.recordFire(kingdomHistory, key, now)
		end
		return effects
	end

	function query.choicePreview(scenarioId: string, responseId: string): ChoicePreview?
		local s = scenarios[scenarioId]
		if s == nil then
			return nil
		end
		for _, r in s.responses do
			if r.id == responseId then
				local e = query.decisionEffects(r.decision)
				if e == nil then
					return nil
				end
				return { decision = r.decision, cost = e.cost, risks = e.risks }
			end
		end
		return nil
	end

	function query.loyaltyDelta(
		rep: RepVector,
		traits: { string },
		relation: Relation,
		chemistry: number?,
		extra: number?
	): number
		local reach = REACH[relation]
		if reach == nil then
			error(`ContentQuery.loyaltyDelta: unknown relation '{tostring(relation)}'`, 2)
		end
		local sum = 0
		for _, traitId in traits do
			local trait = data.traits[traitId]
			if trait == nil then
				error(`ContentQuery.loyaltyDelta: unknown trait '{tostring(traitId)}'`, 2)
			end
			for _, category in CATEGORIES do
				sum += (trait.weights[category] or 0) * (rep[category] or 0)
			end
		end
		return ContentQuery.applyChemistry(sum * reach + (extra or 0), chemistry)
	end

	function query.decisionLoyalty(
		decisionId: string,
		traits: { string },
		relation: Relation,
		chemistry: number?,
		multiplier: number?
	): number
		local d = data.decisions[decisionId]
		if d == nil then
			error(`ContentQuery.decisionLoyalty: unknown decision '{tostring(decisionId)}'`, 2)
		end
		local explicit
		if relation == "speaker" then
			explicit = d.speaker.loyalty
		elseif relation == "family" then
			explicit = d.family_loyalty
		elseif relation == "friends" then
			explicit = d.friends_loyalty
		elseif relation == "rivals" then
			explicit = d.rivals_loyalty
		elseif relation == "kingdom" then
			if d.audience == "none" then
				return 0
			end
			explicit = d.audience_loyalty
		else
			error(`ContentQuery.decisionLoyalty: unknown relation '{tostring(relation)}'`, 2)
		end
		for _, traitId in traits do
			explicit += d.trait_overrides[traitId] or 0
		end
		local delta = query.loyaltyDelta(d.rep, traits, relation, chemistry, explicit)
		return ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta, multiplier or 1), relation)
	end

	local function actionIndices(event: string): { number }
		local out: { number } = {}
		local seen: { [number]: boolean } = {}
		local function add(list: { number }?)
			if list == nil then
				return
			end
			for _, i in list do
				if not seen[i] then
					seen[i] = true
					table.insert(out, i)
				end
			end
		end
		add(data.reputation.byEvent[event])
		local base = string.match(event, "^([^:]+):")
		if base ~= nil then
			add(data.reputation.byEvent[base])
		end
		table.sort(out)
		return out
	end

	function query.actionFirings(event: string, ctx: Ctx?): { ActionFiring }
		local firings: { ActionFiring } = {}
		local byId: { [string]: ActionFiring } = {}
		for _, i in actionIndices(event) do
			local row = data.reputation.actions[i]
			if row == nil or not ContentQuery.evaluate(row.condition, ctx) then
				continue
			end
			local firing = byId[row.id]
			if firing == nil then
				local rep: RepVector = {}
				for _, category in CATEGORIES do
					rep[category] = 0
				end
				local created: ActionFiring = {
					id = row.id,
					farm_key = row.farm_key,
					repeat_decay = row.repeat_decay,
					repeat_window_s = row.repeat_window_s,
					rows = {},
					rep = rep,
					kingdom = { happiness = 0, stability = 0, morale = 0 },
				}
				byId[row.id] = created
				table.insert(firings, created)
				firing = created
			end
			table.insert(firing.rows, row)
			for _, category in CATEGORIES do
				firing.rep[category] += row.rep[category] or 0
			end
			firing.kingdom.happiness += row.kingdom.happiness
			firing.kingdom.stability += row.kingdom.stability
			firing.kingdom.morale += row.kingdom.morale
		end
		return firings
	end

	function query.inActionAudience(row: ActionRow, listener: Listener, listenerCtx: Ctx?): boolean
		local audience = row.audience
		if audience == nil then
			return false
		end
		local occupation = listener.occupation
		local record = if occupation then data.occupations[occupation] else nil
		local job = if record then record.job else nil
		local hears: boolean
		if audience == "speaker" then
			hears = listener.speaker == true
		elseif audience == "kingdom" then
			hears = true
		elseif audience == "soldiers" then
			hears = job == "soldier"
		elseif audience == "civilians" then
			hears = job ~= "soldier"
		else
			local target = string.match(audience, "^occupation:(.+)$")
			hears = target ~= nil and target == occupation
		end
		return hears and ContentQuery.evaluate(row.audience_condition, listenerCtx)
	end

	local function rowRelation(row: ActionRow): Relation
		return if row.audience == "speaker" then "speaker" else "kingdom"
	end

	-- One row's change for one listener, decayed but not clamped (fireAction clamps the listener's sum).
	local function rowLoyalty(row: ActionRow, traits: { string }, chemistry: number?, multiplier: number?): number
		if row.audience == nil then
			return 0
		end
		local delta = query.loyaltyDelta(row.rep, traits, rowRelation(row), chemistry, row.audience_loyalty)
		return ContentQuery.scaleGain(delta, multiplier or 1)
	end

	function query.actionLoyalty(row: ActionRow, traits: { string }, chemistry: number?, multiplier: number?): number
		return ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(rowLoyalty(row, traits, chemistry, multiplier), rowRelation(row))
	end

	function query.fireAction(
		event: string,
		ctx: Ctx?,
		rulerHistory: FarmHistory,
		kingdomHistory: FarmHistory,
		now: number,
		listeners: { ActionListener }?
	): { ActionEffects }
		if type(event) ~= "string" then
			error(`ContentQuery.fireAction: event must be a string, got {typeof(event)}`, 2)
		end
		checkHistory("fireAction", "rulerHistory", rulerHistory)
		checkHistory("fireAction", "kingdomHistory", kingdomHistory)
		checkNow("fireAction", now)
		checkListeners("fireAction", listeners, false)
		local out: { ActionEffects } = {}
		for _, firing in query.actionFirings(event, ctx) do
			local key, decay, window = firing.farm_key, firing.repeat_decay, firing.repeat_window_s
			local m = ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(rulerHistory, key, now, decay, window)
			local km = ContentQuery.repeatMultiplier(kingdomHistory, key, now, decay, window)
			local heard: { ListenerLoyalty } = {}
			for _, listener in listeners or {} do
				local who: Listener = { occupation = listener.occupation, speaker = listener.speaker }
				local total, relation, hears = 0, "kingdom" :: Relation, false
				for _, row in firing.rows do
					if query.inActionAudience(row, who, listener.ctx) then
						hears = true
						if rowRelation(row) == "speaker" then
							relation = "speaker"
						end
						total += rowLoyalty(row, listener.traits, listener.chemistry, km)
					end
				end
				if hears then
					table.insert(heard, {
						citizen = listener.citizen,
						relation = relation,
						loyalty = ContentQuery.clampLoyalty(total, relation),
					})
				end
			end
			-- Decay each row, then sum (model decision 5): a loss in one row is never decayed together with a
			-- gain in another row of the same category, exactly as rowLoyalty treats the listeners.
			local rep: RepVector = {}
			for _, category in CATEGORIES do
				rep[category] = 0
			end
			local kingdom: KingdomDelta = { happiness = 0, stability = 0, morale = 0 }
			for _, row in firing.rows do
				for _, category in CATEGORIES do
					rep[category] += ContentQuery.scaleGain(row.rep[category] or 0, m)
				end
				kingdom.happiness += ContentQuery.scaleGain(row.kingdom.happiness, km)
				kingdom.stability += ContentQuery.scaleGain(row.kingdom.stability, km)
				kingdom.morale += ContentQuery.scaleGain(row.kingdom.morale, km)
			end
			ContentQuery.recordFire(rulerHistory, key, now)
			if kingdomHistory ~= rulerHistory then
				ContentQuery.recordFire(kingdomHistory, key, now)
			end
			table.insert(out, {
				id = firing.id,
				event = event,
				farm_key = key,
				repeat_decay = decay,
				repeat_window_s = window,
				multiplier = m,
				kingdom_multiplier = km,
				rows = firing.rows,
				rep = rep,
				rep_raw = firing.rep,
				kingdom = kingdom,
				kingdom_raw = firing.kingdom,
				listeners = heard,
			})
		end
		return out
	end

	return (query :: any) :: Query
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated content

local default = ContentQuery.new({
	dialogue = (Dialogue :: any) :: DialogueData,
	decisions = (Decisions :: any) :: { [string]: Decision },
	consequences = (Consequences :: any) :: { [string]: Consequence },
	traits = (Traits :: any) :: { [string]: Trait },
	occupations = (Occupations :: any) :: { [string]: Occupation },
	reputation = (Reputation :: any) :: ReputationData,
})

ContentQuery.data = default.data
ContentQuery.eligibleScenarios = default.eligibleScenarios
ContentQuery.choicePreview = default.choicePreview
ContentQuery.decisionEffects = default.decisionEffects
ContentQuery.fireDecision = default.fireDecision
ContentQuery.fireAction = default.fireAction
ContentQuery.loyaltyDelta = default.loyaltyDelta
ContentQuery.decisionLoyalty = default.decisionLoyalty
